On iPhone Duo, Apple includes a display setting for cases or frames that partially cover the left edge of the outer display. It's called Shift Left Edge, and it insets the display edge so that on-screen content isn't hidden beneath the case. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/shift-left-edge-iphone-duo@2x-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1064732" /><br/>
We first <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/iphone-duo-hidden-display-setting-explained/">covered the setting</a> in September, and Apple has since <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/148269">documented</a> it, revealing that when you fit Apple's official <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mkr94zm/a/iphone-duo-case-sand">iPhone Duo Case</a>, a prompt automatically appears on the display to direct you to the setting. However, you can also turn it on manually at any time for third-party cases.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>How to Turn On Shift Left Edge</h2><br/>
<ol><li>Open the Settings app on your iPhone Duo.</li><br/>
<li>Tap <strong>Display & Brightness</strong>.</li><br/>
<li>Toggle on <strong>Shift Left Edge</strong>, then tap <strong>Enable</strong> in the prompt that appears.</li></ol><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/shift-left-edge-setting-duo.jpeg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072895" /><br/>
<br/>
The final prompt will tell you that your iPhone Duo needs to restart to apply the setting, but it's not a full reboot, and you'll be returned to the same settings screen after a brief black screen. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/enable-shift-left-edge-duo.jpeg" alt="settings" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072896" /><br/>
If you subsequently swipe up to the Home Screen, you'll notice a narrow black border on the left side of the outer screen to accommodate the front portion of the case, leaving no content obscured.<br/>
<br/>
